SCOPE CORRECTION (added 2026-07-29, after this commit was pushed).

This commit's message says "Modules + copy + tests" and reads as if ui_strings.js
carried only blueprint/tour copy. It did not. The ui_strings.js change here added
288 keys, of which only 24 are this commit's subject:

  mine (24)   tour.udl_guide_*, tour.universal_settings_*,
              tour.upload_accessibility_*, blueprint.* (archive, fail_*,
              what_is_this, aria/reorder, template_step_count_one, ...)
  swept (264) stem.areaperimeter.* (~230), plus the stem.back / layers_slider /
              off / on / surface_area / volume_label array-to-object
              restructuring (which also accounts for the 6 removed keys), and
              glossary.will_translate / glossary.no_languages_hint

Those 264 belong to a concurrent session's STEM area-perimeter work and were
swept in because they live in the same file. Nothing was lost or overwritten;
the attribution in the message is simply too narrow.

Cause of the bad check: the diff was audited with a line-grep for '"stem.' —
but ui_strings.js is NESTED JSON, so flat dotted keys never appear as literal
text and the grep could not see them. Correct method: flatten both revisions
(JSON.parse + recursive key join) and set-diff the key sets.

Not amended: this commit is already on origin, and amend/reset are disallowed in
this shared working tree.

